    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-029: Flex Layout (Basic)** — `display: flex` / `inline-flex` with single-line algorithm. The ADR that collapses Wikipedia's 585px stacked header to a ~50-100px horizontal bar.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation (3 commits, ~350-400 lines) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n## Why this is the biggest visual delta of the arc\n\n**From ADR-028's layout-tree dump:** `.mw-page-container-inner` starts at y=585. **The entire 585px above it is stacked header blocks** — logo, search, hamburger, dropdown menus, all rendered as full-height children because flex layout isn't implemented. Article content sits at y=633.\n\nWith flex:\n- Header collapses to ~50-100px horizontal bar\n- Article content moves to y≈50-150\n- **485-535px of vertical space reclaimed**\n- Article content finally appears **above the fold**\n\nThat's larger than grid layout's visible delta — grid was invisible until the header height was removed. Flex directly reclaims the largest visible gap.\n\n## Grounded in measurement\n\n### Flex rule distribution (Wikipedia CSS)\n\n**36 flex rules total**: 26 `display: flex`, 10 `display: inline-flex`.\n\n**Property usage across flex containers**:\n\n| Property | Uses |\n|---|---|\n| `display: flex` | 36 |\n| `align-items` | **18** |\n| `justify-content` | 7 |\n| `flex-flow` | 4 |\n| `flex-wrap` | 3 |\n| `gap` | 2 |\n| `flex-direction` | 2 |\n| `flex` (shorthand) | 1 |\n| `flex-shrink` | 1 |\n| `column-gap` | 1 |\n\n**Header-specific rules** driving the visual delta:\n\n```css\n.mw-header {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 16px;\n}\n.mw-header .vector-header-start,\n.mw-header .vector-header-end {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n}\n.vector-header-container {\n    display: flex;\n    justify-content: center;\n}\n```\n\n## What the ADR specifies\n\n### Container properties\n\n- `display: flex` → `Display::Flex`\n- `display: inline-flex` → `Display::InlineFlex` (treated as block-level flex for v1 — visually identical for header case)\n- `flex-direction`: `row` (default) | `column`\n- `justify-content`: `flex-start` | `flex-end` | `center` | `space-between` | `space-around` | `end`\n- `align-items`: `stretch` (default) | `flex-start` | `flex-end` | `center`\n- `gap` / `row-gap` / `column-gap`\n\n### Item properties\n\n- `flex-grow`, `flex-shrink`, `flex-basis` per child\n\n### Shorthand expansion (at parse time, matching ADR-012/028 pattern)\n\n- `flex: <grow> <shrink> <basis>` → 3 longhands\n- `flex-flow: <direction> <wrap>` → 2 longhands\n\n### Algorithm\n\n`layout_flex_children`:\n1. Layout each child at (0,0) for natural size\n2. Compute `flex-basis` per child (explicit length or auto = natural main-axis)\n3. Sum basis + gaps → overflow or remaining\n4. Distribute shrinkage (if overflow) or growth (if remaining) per `flex-grow`/`flex-shrink`\n5. Position along main axis per `justify-content`\n6. Position on cross axis per `align-items` (stretch/flex-start/flex-end/center)\n7. Row/column dispatch based on `flex-direction`\n\n## Three-path prediction (per ADR-027/028 Meta-lesson)\n\n| Path | Status |\n|---|---|\n| **Parse `display: flex`?** | ❌ Falls to `Display::Block` today |\n| **Win cascade?** | ✅ Flex rules are in cascade post-URL-fix |\n| **Consumed by layout?** | ❌ No flex dispatch in `layout_element` |\n\nADR-029 closes **parse + layout-consumption paths**.\n\n## The `flex-wrap` deferral (the biggest scope decision)\n\n**3 rules use `flex-wrap`, including the header's `.mw-header { flex-wrap: wrap }`.**\n\nDeferred because:\n- At 800-1900px viewport widths, the header children (logo + search + hamburger) fit in one line\n- Visual delta from missing wrap is **zero** at typical viewports\n- Multi-line flex requires 2-pass algorithm: break items into lines, then distribute cross-axis across lines\n- **~150 extra lines for a case that doesn't manifest in the target page**\n\n**Alternative** (always treat `wrap` as triggering multi-line): rejected as honest scope discipline — 150 lines for zero visible impact.\n\n**Honest limitation**: at very narrow viewports (<600px), header overflows horizontally instead of wrapping. Documented, deferrable.\n\n## Deferred (enumerated in ADR)\n\n- **`flex-wrap: wrap`** (multi-line flex) — no visible impact at typical viewports\n- `row-reverse`, `column-reverse` — 0 uses\n- `align-self` — 0 uses\n- `align-content` (multi-line only)\n- `order` — 0 uses\n- `inline-flex` as inline-level (treated as block-level flex)\n- Percentage cross-axis `flex-basis`\n- Percentage cross-axis `flex-basis`\n- Percentage cross-axis `flex-basis`\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **`flex-wrap` deferral accepted** — 0 visible impact at typical viewports; multi-line flex is genuinely a separate feature. Comfortable?\n- [ ] **`inline-flex` as block-level flex** — treated as block-level for v1. Only affects elements whose own display must inline-flow; for Wikipedia's header (inline-flex used inside a flex container) behavior is identical either way. Agree?\n- [ ] **`align-items: stretch` implementation** — deferred-ish: compute container cross-axis size after child layout, then stretch items that don't have explicit cross-axis size. Single-pass. Matches header case (children have intrinsic sizes; tallest determines container; no item is stretched).\n- [ ] **Three-path prediction** — high expected delta (485-535px reclaim). Escape hatch committed in ADR: if measured delta is smaller, document honestly (same pattern as every prior ADR this session).\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched, so no test changes. Will run `cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests` after merge to confirm `main` still clean (365 cases, 1508 assertions, unchanged).\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/029-flex-layout.md` — status Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR.\n\nRefs #161\n",
